# Intent: "Use this network now" for a real away test without carrying the unit out of range of the home Wi-Fi (owner 2026-11-14): self.wifi.use_now(index) leaves the current Wi-Fi and joins the chosen saved network. The Wi-Fi component joins the strongest saved network in range (the saved order does not matter), so the choice is a RAM-only hold: only the chosen network is left in the in-memory list the component scans, the saved list in flash is never written, and a restart brings every saved network back. If the hub is not reached on the new network within 3 minutes the full list is restored and the unit reconnects by itself (diagnostic event wifi_use_revert, or wifi_use_ok when the hub was reached and the hold ends). The three tools that add, forget or switch saved networks end a hold first.
# Check after a flash: self.wifi.use_now(index of a hotspot in range) answers {"ok":true,"revert_in_s":180}; the unit joins that network and the hub sees it; self.wifi.list_saved still lists every network afterwards; with the chosen network out of range the unit is back on a saved network about 3 minutes later and the hub receives wifi_use_revert.
